# Solution

## Setup and Transfer Matrix

The 8×8 grid has 9 horizontal lines × 8 segments = 72 horizontal threads, and 9 vertical lines × 8 segments = 72 vertical threads, totaling 144. ✓

I process the grid **row by row**. The state at each row boundary is the 8 horizontal thread colors along that boundary. The transfer matrix $T$ (size $6^8 \times 6^8$) maps the top boundary of a row to its bottom boundary, summing over the 9 vertical threads within the row.

**Face tensor.** For a square with edges $(a, b, l, r)$ = (top, bottom, left, right), define:
$$M[a,b][l,r] = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if } |\{a,b,l,r\}| = 3 \\ 0 & \text{otherwise} \end{cases}$$

This is a 6×6 matrix, symmetric in both pairs: $M[a,b] = M[b,a]$ and $M[a,b]^T = M[a,b]$.

**Transfer matrix entry.** For top row $\mathbf{s} = (s_0,\ldots,s_7)$ and bottom row $\mathbf{s}' = (s_0',\ldots,s_7')$:
$$T[\mathbf{s}, \mathbf{s}'] = \mathbf{1}^T M[s_0,s_0']\, M[s_1,s_1'] \cdots M[s_7,s_7']\, \mathbf{1}$$
where $\mathbf{1}$ is the 6-dimensional all-ones vector. The total count is:
$$N = \mathbf{1}^T T^8 \mathbf{1}$$

## Key Eigenvalue Computation

**Computing $T\mathbf{1}$.** For any fixed $\mathbf{s}$:
$$\sum_{\mathbf{s}'} T[\mathbf{s},\mathbf{s}'] = \mathbf{1}^T \left(\sum_{s_0'} M[s_0,s_0']\right) \cdots \left(\sum_{s_7'} M[s_7,s_7']\right) \mathbf{1}$$

This factorization works because each $s_j'$ appears in exactly one factor, and matrix multiplication distributes over addition in each factor independently.

Define $P(c) = \sum_b M[c,b]$. By $S_6$ symmetry, $P(c) = P$ for all $c$. Computing $P$ (fixing $c=1$):

| Entry condition | Value |
|---|---|
| $P[1,1]$: $\{a,1,1,1\}$ needs 3 distinct | 0 |
| $P[1,j]$, $j\neq 1$: $\{a,1,1,j\}$ needs 3 distinct → $a \notin\{1,j\}$ | 4 |
| $P[i,i]$, $i\neq 1$: $\{a,1,i,i\}$ needs 3 distinct → $a \notin\{1,i\}$ | 4 |
| $P[i,j]$, $i\neq j$, both $\neq 1$: $\{a,1,i,j\}$ already has 3 distinct → $a\in\{1,i,j\}$ | 3 |

